STM32CubeH7P
############

Origin:
   STMicroelectronics
   https://www.st.com/en/embedded-software/stm32cubeh7p.html

Status:
   version 2.0.0

Purpose:
   STMicroelectronics official MCU package for STM32H7P series.

Description:
   This package is an extract of official STM32CubeH7P package written by STMicroelectronics.
   It is composed of STM32Cube hardware abstraction layer (HAL) and low layer (LL) plus a set
   of CMSIS headers files, one for each SoC in the STM32H7P series.

Dependencies:
   None.

URL:
   https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/STM32CubeH7P

Commit:
   94982c0018262122ada273271aa5a9e1b5b404e4

Maintained-by:
   External

License:
   BSD-3-Clause

License Link:
   https://opensource.org/licenses/BSD-3-Clause

Patch List:
   *Changes from official delivery:
    -dos2unix applied
    -trailing white spaces removed

   *Disable HAL UCPD module
      -The HAL UCPD module depends on the HAL DMA module which is not
       always enabled in Zephyr. Since it is never used, as the Zephyr
       driver for UCPD uses the LL API, disable the module completely
       to avoid build errors.
      -Impacted files:
         - stm32cube/stm32h7pxx/drivers/templates/common/stm32h7pxx_hal_conf.h

   *Make HAL DMA usage conditional
      -Allow the USE_HAL_DMA_MODULE configuration option to come from the
       compiler flags (-DUSE_HAL_DMA_MODULE=0/1), and enable DMA mode in
       all other HAL modules only if the HAL DMA module itself is enabled.
      -Impacted files:
         - stm32cube/stm32h7pxx/drivers/templates/common/stm32h7pxx_hal_conf.h
